shooting-15\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#workspace-lock-is-held\",\"content\":\"Another `run` or non-dry `run --watch` is active for the same Workspace.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-16\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-16\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#workspace-lock-is-held\",\"content\":\"Fix: stop the other process. Do not delete `run.lock` while a process is running.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-17\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-17\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#required-command-qmd-not-found\",\"content\":\"The Workspace has a QMD Source, but `qmd` is not on `PATH`.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-18\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-18\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#required-command-qmd-not-found\",\"content\":\"Fix: install QMD or remove the QMD Source from the Workspace.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-19\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-19\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#required-command-git-not-found\",\"content\":\"The Workspace uses `@clankpipe/action-worktree`, but `git` is not on `PATH`.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-20\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-20\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#required-command-git-not-found\",\"content\":\"Fix: install Git or remove that Action.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-21\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-21\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#action-keeps-retrying\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe retries failed Actions until one succeeds for the same retry identity:\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-22\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-22\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#action-keeps-retrying\",\"content\":\"Fix the command, credentials, paths, or Source item data. Then run again.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-23\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-23\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#worktree-action-refused-an-existing-root\",\"content\":\"`@clankpipe/action-worktree` only manages an exact worktree root from the configured `repo`. It reuses the requested branch, but refuses to switch dirty worktrees or a branch checked out in another worktree.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-24\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-24\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#worktree-action-refused-an-existing-root\",\"content\":\"Fix the `repo` or `root`, commit or remove tracked and untracked changes, or release the requested branch from its other worktree. The Action never forces, resets, or cleans a worktree.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-25\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-25\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#environment-variable-did-not-expand\",\"content\":\"First identify where expansion belongs.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-26\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-26\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#environment-variable-did-not-expand\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe expands leading `~/`, `$VAR`, and `${VAR}` after MiniJinja rendering only for path inputs:\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-27\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-27\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#environment-variable-did-not-expand\",\"content\":\"`@clankpipe/action-run-cmd.cwd`\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-28\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-28\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#environment-variable-did-not-expand\",\"content\":\"`@clankpipe/action-worktree.repo`\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-29\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-29\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#environment-variable-did-not-expand\",\"content\":\"`@clankpipe/action-worktree.root`\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-30\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-30\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#environment-variable-did-not-expand\",\"content\":\"For these fields, check that the variable exists in the environment of the `clankpipe` process, not only an interactive shell startup file.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-31\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-31\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#environment-variable-did-not-expand\",\"content\":\"Variables in `@clankpipe/action-run-cmd.cmd` and `healthcheck` are left literal until `sh -c` runs. The shell starts in the configured `cwd`, so `$PWD` resolves there. Check shell syntax, quoting, exported variables, and whether the shell process receives the expected environment.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-32\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-32\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#environment-variable-did-not-expand\",\"content\":\"MiniJinja expressions such as `{{ item.reference_id }}` always render before either kind of environment expansion.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-33\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-33\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#jira-credentials-fail\",\"content\":\"For environment variables, check:\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-34\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-34\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#jira-credentials-fail\",\"content\":\"For credential helpers, check that the helper prints one username key and one password key:\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-35\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-35\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#jira-credentials-fail\",\"content\":\"Accepted username keys: `username`, `email`.\\nAccepted password keys: `password`, `token`.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-36\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-36\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#bad-toml-or-unknown-field\",\"content\":\"Workspace config denies unknown fields, including inputs under `[sources.actions.with]` that the selected Action does not declare.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-37\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-37\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#bad-toml-or-unknown-field\",\"content\":\"Use the schema:\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-38\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-38\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#list-shows-unexpected-items\",\"content\":\"`list` shows the latest committed Source Snapshot for each configured Source. It does not show older observations that are not members of that Snapshot.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-39\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-39\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#list-shows-unexpected-items\",\"content\":\"If the Snapshot is missing, run the Workspace successfully. If an Item remains unexpected, inspect the Source query and the matching Snapshot records in the Store.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-40\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-40\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#migration-from-agentboard\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe replaces AgentBoard. The old `agentboard` executable remains available as a compatibility alias.\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-41\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-41\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#migration-from-agentboard\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe accepts old `agentboard` configuration and data paths. The compatibility alias remains through the 0.x release line. The project will remove it in the first stable major release. Rename these paths when you migrate a workspace:\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-42\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-42\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#migration-from-agentboard\",\"content\":\"`.agentboard.toml` to `.clankpipe.toml`\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-43\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-43\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#migration-from-agentboard\",\"content\":\"`agentboard.config.ts` or `agentboard.config.js` to `clankpipe.config.ts` or `clankpipe.config.js`\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-44\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-44\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#migration-from-agentboard\",\"content\":\"`~/.config/agentboard` to `~/.config/clankpipe`\"}],[\"/cli/troubleshooting-45\",{\"id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting-45\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/troubleshooting\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/troubleshooting#migration-from-agentboard\",\"content\":\"`~/.local/share/agentboard` to `~/.local/share/clankpipe`\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"Workspaces\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"ClankPipe\",\"Cli\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-0\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-0\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#workspaces\",\"content\":\"Workspaces\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-1\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-1\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#file-selection\",\"content\":\"File selection\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-2\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-2\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#minimal-shape\",\"content\":\"Minimal shape\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-3\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-3\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#validation\",\"content\":\"Validation\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-4\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-4\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#source-and-action-docs\",\"content\":\"Source and Action docs\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-5\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-5\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#workspaces\",\"content\":\"A Workspace is one TOML file. It names Sources and the Actions for each Source.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-6\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-6\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#file-selection\",\"content\":\"Operational commands use `.clankpipe.toml` in the current directory when no Workspace argument is provided:\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-7\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-7\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#file-selection\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe does not search parent directories. A supplied path selects exactly one file. ClankPipe does not merge files, load profiles, or apply field-level CLI overrides.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-8\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-8\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#file-selection\",\"content\":\"Named Workspaces are not resolved by operational commands. `workspace list` only lists `*.toml` files under the platform config directory. Pass the listed file path to another command:\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-9\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-9\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#file-selection\",\"content\":\"The config directory follows the platform. On Linux, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` sets the base directory; otherwise ClankPipe uses `~/.config`. ClankPipe adds the `clankpipe` directory below that base.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-10\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-10\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#file-selection\",\"content\":\"The Workspace id uses the canonical path, so moving a Workspace creates a different Store location.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-11\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-11\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#minimal-shape\",\"content\":\"A Source id must be a non-empty unique string. A Source can omit `actions`; this means that no Action runs and the Store reports the Action plan as successful.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-12\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-12\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#minimal-shape\",\"content\":\"Each Source package owns its fields. Each Action package owns the fields under `[sources.actions.with]`. Unknown fields fail Workspace validation. Action input values are strings in data Workspaces.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-13\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-13\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#validation\",\"content\":\"Validation has two layers:\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-14\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-14\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#validation\",\"content\":\"Workspace loading checks TOML structure, required fields, types, plugin names, unknown fields, Source ids, and Action ids.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-15\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-15\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#validation\",\"content\":\"`doctor` and the normal Run path perform package-specific validation and environment checks.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-16\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-16\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#validation\",\"content\":\"Action ids are optional. When present, an Action id must match `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*` and be unique within its Source. Later named Actions can use the id in templates.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-17\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-17\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#validation\",\"content\":\"`clankpipe schema` describes structural fields and types. It does not express every runtime rule. Use `doctor` to test the configured environment.\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-18\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-18\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#source-and-action-docs\",\"content\":\"QMD source\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-19\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-19\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#source-and-action-docs\",\"content\":\"Jira source\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-20\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-20\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#source-and-action-docs\",\"content\":\"GitHub source\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-21\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-21\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#source-and-action-docs\",\"content\":\"`@clankpipe/action-worktree`\"}],[\"/cli/workspaces-22\",{\"id\":\"/cli/workspaces-22\",\"page_id\":\"/cli/workspaces\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/cli/workspaces#source-and-action-docs\",\"content\":\"`@clankpipe/action-run-cmd`\"}],[\"/sources/github\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"GitHub source\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"ClankPipe\",\"Sources\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/github\"}],[\"/sources/github-0\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-0\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/github#github-source\",\"content\":\"GitHub source\"}],[\"/sources/github-1\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-1\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/github#identity-reference-and-status\",\"content\":\"Identity, reference, and status\"}],[\"/sources/github-2\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-2\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/github#credentials\",\"content\":\"Credentials\"}],[\"/sources/github-3\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-3\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#github-source\",\"content\":\"Use `uses = \\\"@clankpipe/source-github\\\"` with `mode = \\\"issue\\\"` to collect GitHub issues through GitHub issue search.\"}],[\"/sources/github-4\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-4\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#github-source\",\"content\":\"`mode`, `query`, `credentials`, and a non-empty `status_map` are required. Issue mode sends `query` to GitHub GraphQL `ISSUE_ADVANCED` search and adds `state:open type:issue`. This supports GitHub advanced search syntax, including grouped `OR` expressions, while excluding pull requests.\"}],[\"/sources/github-5\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-5\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#github-source\",\"content\":\"`limit` defaults to 50. `field_map` is optional. Each `status_map` key matches an issue label or the GitHub state, and its value becomes the normalized Item status.\"}],[\"/sources/github-6\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-6\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#identity-reference-and-status\",\"content\":\"Issue mode uses `owner/repo#number` as `item.id` and the issue number as\\n`item.reference_id`. This keeps equal issue numbers from different repositories\\ndistinct while templates can use the normal GitHub issue number.\"}],[\"/sources/github-7\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-7\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#identity-reference-and-status\",\"content\":\"Status comes from the first matching `status_map` entry on the issue labels. If no label matches, status falls back to the GitHub issue state.\"}],[\"/sources/github-8\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-8\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#identity-reference-and-status\",\"content\":\"Use `field_map` only when the default normalized fields are wrong for a workspace.\"}],[\"/sources/github-9\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-9\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#identity-reference-and-status\",\"content\":\"`field_map.id` changes `item.reference_id`; it does not change `item.id`. Issue mode keeps the REST field names `html_url` and `repository_url` available for field maps while it uses GraphQL internally.\"}],[\"/sources/github-10\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-10\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#identity-reference-and-status\",\"content\":\"Use `status_map` to normalize GitHub issue labels to workspace status values.\"}],[\"/sources/github-11\",{\"id\":\"/sources/github-11\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/github\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/github#credentials\",\"content\":\"The credential helper is any command that writes a token to stdout. `gh auth token` is the common human-friendly helper, but any secret manager command can be used.\"}],[\"/sources/jira\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"Jira source\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"ClankPipe\",\"Sources\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/jira\"}],[\"/sources/jira-0\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-0\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/jira#jira-source\",\"content\":\"Jira source\"}],[\"/sources/jira-1\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-1\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"Field mapping\"}],[\"/sources/jira-2\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-2\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#jira-source\",\"content\":\"Use `uses = \\\"@clankpipe/source-jira\\\"` to collect Jira issues with JQL.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-3\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-3\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#jira-source\",\"content\":\"Credentials come from environment variables by default. Defaults are `JIRA_EMAIL`\\nand `JIRA_API_TOKEN`.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-4\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-4\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#jira-source\",\"content\":\"Or configure a credential helper. ClankPipe writes Git-style request lines to\\nstdin (`protocol`, `host`) and reads either `username`/`password` or\\n`email`/`token` lines from stdout.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-5\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-5\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe uses Jira's internal issue `id` as stable `item.id` inside the Jira\\nsite's Item Store. The Jira issue key is the default `item.reference_id`.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-6\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-6\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"Defaults map `reference_id` from `key`, `title` from `fields.summary`, `status`\\nfrom `fields.status.name`, and `url` to `{site}/browse/{key}`. Override mappings\\nwhen you need custom Jira fields. Use `status_map` to normalize Jira status names.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-7\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-7\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe automatically requests Jira fields referenced by mapping paths that\\nstart with `fields.`. For example, `fields.customfield_10010.value` requests\\nthe top-level Jira field `customfield_10010`.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-8\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-8\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"`field_map.id` changes `item.reference_id`; it does not change `item.id`.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-9\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-9\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"Use `status_map` when Jira's status names should normalize to ClankPipe statuses.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-10\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-10\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"Use `fields` only for extra Jira API fields you want preserved in the raw\\npayload but do not use in `field_map`.\"}],[\"/sources/qmd\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"QMD source\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"ClankPipe\",\"Sources\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/qmd\"}],[\"/sources/qmd-0\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd-0\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/qmd#qmd-source\",\"content\":\"QMD source\"}],[\"/sources/qmd-1\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd-1\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/qmd#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"Field mapping\"}],[\"/sources/qmd-2\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd-2\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/qmd#qmd-source\",\"content\":\"Use `uses = \\\"@clankpipe/source-qmd\\\"` to collect items from QMD collections.\"}],[\"/sources/qmd-3\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd-3\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/qmd#qmd-source\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe runs `qmd query --format json --full -n <limit>` and reads each result's raw\\ndocument body. It passes each configured collection with `-c <collection>`. Each matched note must have YAML frontmatter with string values at the paths configured by `map` for `id`, `title`, and `status`. `url` is optional; when absent ClankPipe uses the QMD document reference.\"}],[\"/sources/qmd-4\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd-4\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/qmd#qmd-source\",\"content\":\"`collections` and `query` are required. `limit` defaults to 50 and must be positive. `map` is optional and defaults to the paths `id`, `title`, `status`, and `url`.\"}],[\"/sources/qmd-5\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd-5\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/qmd#qmd-source\",\"content\":\"The QMD document reference is `item.id`. The mapped frontmatter `id` is\\n`item.reference_id`, so moving reference mapping does not change Store or Action\\nidentity.\"}],[\"/sources/qmd-6\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd-6\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/qmd#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"Use `map` when your frontmatter uses different names or nested fields.\"}],[\"/sources/qmd-7\",{\"id\":\"/sources/qmd-7\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/qmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/qmd#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"`map.id` changes `item.reference_id`; it does not change `item.id`.\"}],[\"/actions/llm\",{\"id\":\"/actions/llm\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/llm\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"LLM action\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"ClankPipe\",\"Actions\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/actions/llm\"}],[\"/actions/llm-0\",{\"id\":\"/actions/llm-0\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/llm\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/llm\",\"content\":\"Use `@clankpipe/action-llm` to run a Pi prompt directly or in a terminal.\"}],[\"/actions/llm-1\",{\"id\":\"/actions/llm-1\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/llm\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/llm\",\"content\":\"Set exactly one of `prompt` or `prompt_file`. The prompt file path is read after\\nClankPipe renders action inputs.\"}],[\"/actions/llm-2\",{\"id\":\"/actions/llm-2\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/llm\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/llm\",\"content\":\"Use `worktree` to create or reuse a clean Git worktree before the agent starts.\\nThe action does not switch an existing worktree to another branch.\"}],[\"/actions/llm-3\",{\"id\":\"/actions/llm-3\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/llm\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/llm\",\"content\":\"Set `terminal` to `zellij`, `herdr`, `tmux`, or `generic`. Set `harness` to the\\nagent harness executable and `harness_args` to its arguments. The rendered\\nprompt is the final harness argument. Pi starts a new saved session by default.\\nConfigure `--session-id` or `--no-session` explicitly when you need different behavior. Direct launches wait for Pi in\\n`foreground` mode. Direct `background` launches return `running` immediately\\nand ClankPipe records the final result when the child exits.\"}],[\"/actions/llm-4\",{\"id\":\"/actions/llm-4\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/llm\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/llm\",\"content\":\"Terminal launchers return `running` after they accept the command. Herdr\\nworktree launches create a new tab in the worktree workspace. Herdr, Zellij,\\nand tmux do not expose agent completion to this Action. ClankPipe\\nmarks such executions `stale (disconnected)` during recovery unless a later\\nAction execution records completion.\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"Run command action\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"ClankPipe\",\"Actions\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-0\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-0\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"Run Command Action\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-1\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-1\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"Use `@clankpipe/action-run-cmd` to run a shell command for each collected item.\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-2\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-2\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"ClankPipe runs the command through `sh -c`. Templates can use the collected\\nitem and source fields.\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-3\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-3\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"The command receives these environment variables:\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-4\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-4\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"`CLANKPIPE_WORKSPACE_ID`\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-5\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-5\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"`CLANKPIPE_SOURCE_ID`\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-6\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-6\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"`CLANKPIPE_ITEM_ID`\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-7\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-7\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"The old `AGENTBOARD_*` names remain available as aliases.\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-8\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-8\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"Set `cwd` when the command should run from a specific directory.\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-9\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-9\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"For asynchronous launch commands, set `healthcheck` to a shell probe that\\nreports readiness with exit status `0`. ClankPipe runs the probe immediately\\nafter a successful launch, then polls until it passes or times out.\"}],[\"/actions/run-cmd-10\",{\"id\":\"/actions/run-cmd-10\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/run-cmd\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/run-cmd#run-command-action\",\"content\":\"The interval defaults to `1s`; the timeout defaults to `30s`. Both accept\\nhuman-readable durations such as `250ms`, `5s`, or `2m`. The healthcheck uses\\nthe same `cwd` and ClankPipe environment variables as `cmd`. A launch failure\\nskips the healthcheck. A timeout fails the action, so a later run retries it.\"}],[\"/actions/worktree\",{\"id\":\"/actions/worktree\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/worktree\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"Worktree action\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"ClankPipe\",\"Actions\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/actions/worktree\"}],[\"/actions/worktree-0\",{\"id\":\"/actions/worktree-0\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/worktree\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/actions/worktree#worktree-action\",\"content\":\"Worktree action\"}],[\"/actions/worktree-1\",{\"id\":\"/actions/worktree-1\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/worktree\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/worktree#worktree-action\",\"content\":\"Use `@clankpipe/action-worktree` to ensure each item has a Git worktree on its\\nrequested branch. The Action creates an absent worktree, reuses a matching\\nworktree, or safely switches a clean managed worktree.\"}],[\"/actions/worktree-2\",{\"id\":\"/actions/worktree-2\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/worktree\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/worktree#worktree-action\",\"content\":\"`repo` is the source repository. `root` is a separate worktree path. `branch`\\nis a local branch name to create or switch to for the item. Existing roots must\\nbe exact worktree roots from `repo`; switching refuses tracked or untracked\\nchanges and branches already checked out elsewhere.\"}],[\"/actions/worktree-3\",{\"id\":\"/actions/worktree-3\",\"page_id\":\"/actions/worktree\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/actions/worktree#worktree-action\",\"content\":\"Pair it with `@clankpipe/action-run-cmd` when you want to open the new worktree in a\\nterminal or agent session.\"}]]"}}